**Read:** [Outdoor polymer service-life inference — Duan and colleagues](../sources/Polymer-Service-Life-Duan-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_06S8ZC7PTSPQYJJTFMH97NFFTT), outdoor prediction and threshold discussion; [Spacecraft polymer atomic-oxygen durability — NASA-HDBK-6024](../sources/Atomic-Oxygen-Durability-NASA.lingua#r_1RMMZEYQQCZ08VRYTHCQBEEHJ0), flight comparisons; [Alkali-Aggregate Reactivity Facts Book — FHWA](../sources/Alkali-Aggregate-Reactivity-FHWA.lingua#r_1RPCXTH7BRN45SFFG6XC76WZNK), diagnosis/prognosis.

A degradation signal is not necessarily the required function. Define failure as a stated loss of optical, mechanical, barrier or other performance, with a defensible relation to the measured response. Some specimens survive the observation period; others are removed for reasons unrelated to deterioration. These observations are censored or selected, not simply absent failures.

**Work:** Reconstruct exposure histories and observation schedules for laboratory and service specimens. Keep fitting data separate from prediction data and distinguish specimen variability from parameter uncertainty. Evaluate a functional threshold against independent measurements, then show how its uncertainty affects life estimates. Explain the consequences of ignoring surviving specimens, undocumented maintenance or a change in formulation during the study.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
